{#-
  Spiko: subscribe to a Spiko fund with a stablecoin, and redeem the fund
  token back into that stablecoin.

  Subscription. Spiko assigns each account a deposit address. Stablecoins
  sent there are invested in the fund at the next NAV, and Spiko mints the
  fund token to the account's wallet in a later transaction. The Safe only
  needs a plain ERC-20 `transfer`.

  Redemption starts on-chain from the Safe, which sends the fund token to
  one of Spiko's two redemption contracts. `redeem_via` picks the route
  Spiko serves for `fund`:

    multi_atm           Spiko's MultiATM swaps the fund token into the
                        payment asset in the same transaction, at Spiko's
                        oracle price. The Safe approves the ATM, then calls
                        `swapExactInputSingle`. A swap is bounded by the
                        ATM's payment-asset balance. Only pairs Spiko
                        registered on the ATM work (mainnet: USTBL/USDC; no
                        SAFO pair).

    redemption_request  The Safe `transferAndCall`s the fund token to
                        Spiko's Redemption contract with
                        `abi.encode(output, salt)`, which opens a request in
                        the Safe's name. Spiko executes it (burns the fund
                        tokens) and pays the output in a later transaction,
                        off this contract. A request not executed within 14
                        days can be cancelled by anyone, which returns the
                        fund tokens to the Safe. Only outputs Spiko registered
                        for the fund work (`outputsFor`; mainnet: SAFO →
                        USDC; USTBL → fiat only).

  A route Spiko does not serve for the fund reverts on-chain (`UnknownPair`
  on the ATM, "Input/Output pair is not authorized" on Redemption): the grant
  is inert, not wider. Spiko also gates both routes: the Safe must be
  whitelisted on the fund token, and on the ATM for multi_atm.

  The ATM pays whatever `recipient` the caller names, so `recipient` is
  pinned to the Safe. Redemption records the caller (the Safe) as the
  request's owner, and `output` is pinned to the payment asset: the zero
  address requests fiat, paid outside the chain.

  The role gets exactly:
    payment asset  transfer(to in subscription_addresses, value: any)
    multi_atm
      fund         approve(spender == MultiATM, amount: any)
      MultiATM     swapExactInputSingle(input == fund, output == payment asset,
                   inputAmount: any, recipient == Safe, minOutputAmount: any)
    redemption_request
      fund         transferAndCall(to == Redemption, value: any,
                   data == abi.encode(output == payment asset, salt: any))
  No other selector on the fund token, so the fund token can only leave the
  Safe toward Spiko. No multi-hop or exact-output swap, no ETH, no
  delegatecall.

  Params
    payment_asset          Token alias key, e.g. "USDC". Resolved via
                           aliases.tokens[<key>]; unknown key fails at render.
                           The asset subscribed with and redeemed into.
    subscription_addresses Deposit addresses Spiko assigned to this account,
                           usually one. Each entry is a place the payment asset
                           can leave the Safe with no further approval, so list
                           only addresses Spiko actually assigned. Literals or
                           deployment-local aliases, not curated ones.
    fund                   Spiko fund alias key, e.g. "USTBL". Resolved via
                           aliases.spiko.funds[<key>]; unknown key fails at
                           render.
    redeem_via             "multi_atm" or "redemption_request". Required: a
                           subscription without a redemption route leaves the
                           role no way out of the position. Anything else fails
                           at render.

  Resolved from aliases (not params)
    aliases.spiko.multi_atm   MultiATM
    aliases.spiko.redemption  Redemption

  Output
    All functions execution_options "none".
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- if redeem_via is not defined or (redeem_via != "multi_atm" and redeem_via != "redemption_request") -%}
  {{ spiko_error_redeem_via_must_be_multi_atm_or_redemption_request }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set fund_address = aliases.spiko.funds[fund] -%}
{%- set payment_address = aliases.tokens[payment_asset] -%}
roles:
  - address: "{{ payment_address }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function transfer(address to, uint256 value)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: to
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for addr in subscription_addresses %}
              - "{{ addr }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: value
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
{%- if redeem_via == "multi_atm" %}

  {{ approve(fund_address, aliases.spiko.multi_atm) | indent(2) }}

  - address: "{{ aliases.spiko.multi_atm }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function swapExactInputSingle(address input, address output, uint256 inputAmount, address recipient, uint256 minOutputAmount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: input
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ fund_address }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: output
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ payment_address }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: inputAmount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: recipient
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: minOutputAmount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
{%- else %}

  - address: "{{ fund_address }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function transferAndCall(address to, uint256 value, bytes data)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: to
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.spiko.redemption }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: value
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: data
            param_type: "abi_encoded"
            children:
              - name: output
                param_type: "static"
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ payment_address }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: salt
                param_type: "static"
                operator: "pass"
                value_type: "bytes32"
{%- endif %}
